</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Related work comparison ‣ Distributional Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we compare DistIRL with existing IRL methods along four key dimensions. The first column, <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Model reward distribution</span>, asks whether a method explicitly represents the reward as a random variable rather than as a fixed deterministic function. For example, Bayesian IRL methods place a prior over reward parameters, thereby modeling uncertainty, but they do not recover the actual shape of the underlying distribution. This is distinct from <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recover reward distribution</span>, which requires learning the full distribution of rewards themselves, including higher-order statistics such as variance and skewness, rather than just a posterior over parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The third column, <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Infer risk-aware policy</span>, evaluates whether a method incorporates risk measures into policy inference. Methods in this category optimize beyond expected return, often capturing aversion or preference to variability in outcomes. The final column, <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Learn return distribution</span>, indicates whether a method leverages distributional reinforcement learning (DistRL) techniques to estimate the full distribution of returns, rather than only their expectation. Unlike reward distributions, which describe stochasticity at the immediate reward level, return distributions capture the cumulative effect of randomness from rewards, transitions, and policies over trajectories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in the table, most prior IRL methods either assume deterministic rewards or restrict themselves to expectation-based inference. In contrast, DistIRL is the first framework that simultaneously models stochastic rewards, learns full reward distributions, integrates distributional return estimation, and supports risk-aware policy learning, thereby unifying these capabilities in a principled way.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first wish to show that</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)]_{+}dz=\int_{0}^{1}\bigl[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\bigr]_{+}{d}v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)]_{+}dz=\int_{0}^{1}\bigl[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\bigr]_{+}{d}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> be two real-valued integrable random variables with cumulative distribution functions <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Z^{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Z^{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Z^{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Z^{E}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and corresponding quantile functions <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)\right]_{+}\,dz=\int_{0}^{1}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\right]_{+}\,dv," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)\right]_{+}\,dz=\int_{0}^{1}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\right]_{+}\,dv,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x]_{+}:=\max(x,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x]_{+}:=\max(x,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)\right]_{+}dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)-F_{Z^{E}}(z)\right]_{+}dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)\geq v,v\geq F_{Z^{E}}(z)}dvdz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)\geq v,v\geq F_{Z^{E}}(z)}dvdz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)\geq v,v\geq F_{Z^{E}}(z)}dvdz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}(z)\geq v,v\geq F_{Z^{E}}(z)}dvdz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)\geq z,z\geq F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)}dvdz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathbbm{1}_{F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)\geq z,z\geq F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)}dvdz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\right]_{+}dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left[F_{Z^{\pi}}^{-1}(v)-F_{Z^{E}}^{-1}(v)\right]_{+}dv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The interchange of integrals are permitted by the Theorem of Fubini-Tonelli as everything is positive <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heil, 2019</a>)</cite>. Note that the definition of the quantile function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gut &amp; Gut, 2006</a>)</cite> is:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F^{-1}(v):=\inf_{z\in\mathbb{R}}\{F(z)\geq v\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{-1}(v):=\inf_{z\in\mathbb{R}}\{F(z)\geq v\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmdefinition6" title="Proposition 4.6. ‣ 4.2 Risk-aware Policy Learning ‣ 4 Distributional Inverse Reinforcement Learning Framework ‣ Distributional Inverse Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the difference in quantile functions:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(v):=F_{X}^{-1}(v)-F_{Y}^{-1}(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(v):=F_{X}^{-1}(v)-F_{Y}^{-1}(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose for contradiction that the set</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\{v\in[0,1]\mid h(v)&lt;0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\{v\in[0,1]\mid h(v)&lt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">has positive Borel measure, i.e., <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(A)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(A)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let’s define a distortion function <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> whose derivative is:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{A}^{\prime}(v)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\mu(A)}&amp;\text{if }v\in A,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{A}^{\prime}(v)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\mu(A)}&amp;\text{if }v\in A,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid distortion function and satisfies <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}d\tilde{\xi}_{A}(v)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}d\tilde{\xi}_{A}(v)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{{\xi}_{A}}(X)-\mathcal{M}_{{\xi}_{A}}(Y)=\int_{0}^{1}h(v)\,d\tilde{\xi}_{A}(v)=\int_{A}h(v)\cdot\frac{1}{\mu(A)}\,dv&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{{\xi}_{A}}(X)-\mathcal{M}_{{\xi}_{A}}(Y)=\int_{0}^{1}h(v)\,d\tilde{\xi}_{A}(v)=\int_{A}h(v)\cdot\frac{1}{\mu(A)}\,dv&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This contradicts the assumption that <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\tilde{\xi}}(X)\geq\mathcal{M}_{\tilde{\xi}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\tilde{\xi}}(X)\geq\mathcal{M}_{\tilde{\xi}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> for all distortion functions <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the set where <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{X}^{-1}(v)&lt;F_{Y}^{-1}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{X}^{-1}(v)&lt;F_{Y}^{-1}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> must have measure zero.
Thus we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{X}^{-1}(v)\geq F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\quad\text{for }v\in[0,1]\text{ almost everywhere (a.e.)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> almost everywhere (a.e.)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{X}^{-1}(v)\geq F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\quad\text{for }v\in[0,1]\text{ almost everywhere (a.e.)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{X}(z)\leq F_{Y}(z)\quad\text{for all }z\in\mathbb{R}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{X}(z)\leq F_{Y}(z)\quad\text{for all }z\in\mathbb{R},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">since</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{X}(z)=P_{X}\left(X&lt;z\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{X}(z)=P_{X}\left(X&lt;z\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)+\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)+\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\left(\{v\in[0,1]|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=F_{Y}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=F_{Y}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">The second inequality is due to the fact that for any <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\subseteq\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{X}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}\subseteq\{v\in[0,1]\cap A^{c}|F_{Y}^{-1}(v)\leq z\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\succeq_{\text{FSD}}Y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⪰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>FSD</mtext></msub><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\succeq_{\text{FSD}}Y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Model architecture and hyper-parameters</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we use the following model architecture for all the experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Model Parameters for DistIRL</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A3.T6.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Parameters</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Learning Rate</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Batch Size</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">512</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Total Iterations</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">5,000</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Entropy Coefficient</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.1</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Risk Measure</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">CVaR</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Risk Parameter</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.05</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Reward Regularization</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.01</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="A3.T6.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Network Architecture</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Policy Network</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">[256, 128]</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Distribution Type</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Skew Gaussian</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Reward Range</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">[-5.0, 5.0]</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Number of Quantiles</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">200</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">Reward Hidden Features</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">128</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For gridworld, we specify the reward range as <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math>. For MuJoCo tasks, <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-10,10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-10,10]</annotation></semantics></math>. This is achieved by applying a (scaled) tanh function.</p>
</div>
</section>
